(window.FBDI_SPECS = window.FBDI_SPECS || {})["StandardCostImportTemplate"] = {"zip":"CstStandardCostImport","end":1,"sheets":[{"n":"CST_INTERFACE_STD_COST_HEADERS","csv":"CstStdCostHeadersInterface","cols":[{"n":"External System Reference","c":"EXTERNAL_SYSTEM_REFERENCE","t":"V","r":1,"h":"External System Reference"},{"n":"External System Reference Identifier","c":"EXTERNAL_SYSTEM_REF_ID","t":"V","r":1,"h":"External System Identifier"},{"n":"Scenario Number","c":"SCENARIO_NUMBER","t":"V","r":1,"h":"Scenario Number"},{"n":"Item Number","c":"ITEM_NUMBER","t":"V","r":1,"h":"Item Number"},{"n":"Valuation Unit Code","c":"VAL_UNIT_CODE","t":"V","r":1,"h":"Valuation Unit Code"},{"n":"Cost Organization","c":"COST_ORG_CODE","t":"V","h":"Cost Organization Name"},{"n":"Cost Book","c":"COST_BOOK_CODE","t":"V","h":"Cost Book"},{"n":"Buy Cost","c":"BUY_COST_FLAG","t":"V","h":"Buy Cost"}],"ex":[]},{"n":"CST_INTERFACE_STD_COST_DETAILS","csv":"CstStdCostDetailsInterface","cols":[{"n":"External System Reference","c":"EXTERNAL_SYSTEM_REFERENCE","t":"V","r":1,"h":"External System Reference"},{"n":"External System Reference Identifier","c":"EXTERNAL_SYSTEM_REF_ID","t":"V","r":1,"h":"External System Identifier"},{"n":"Line Number","c":"LINE_NUMBER","t":"N","p":"18","r":1,"h":"Line Number idetiifing a unique detail record with respect to a standard cost header"},{"n":"Cost Element Set Code","c":"COST_ELEMENT_SET_CODE","t":"V","r":1,"h":"Cost Element Set Code"},{"n":"Cost Element Code","c":"COST_ELEMENT_CODE","t":"V","r":1,"h":"Cost Element Code"},{"n":"Expense Pool Set Code","c":"EXPENSE_POOL_SET_CODE","t":"V","h":"Cost Element Set Code"},{"n":"Expense Pool Code","c":"","t":"V"},{"n":"Unit Cost","c":"UNIT_COST","t":"N","r":1,"h":"Unit Cost"}],"ex":[]}],"ins":["Fusion Applications 11g Release 8 (11.1.8)","Standard Cost Open Interface - Define Standard Costs","Overview","You can use the Standard Costing Open Interface to upload standard costs in bulk to Oracle Fusion Cost Management.  This template has separate tabs on which you may enter the appropriate header and details information. The standard cost open interface requires the following tables created in a parent-child relationship in order to define a standard cost:\n\n- The table CST_INTERFACE_STD_COST_HEADERS contains the standard cost header information, such as Cost Organization, Cost Book, Item Number, V","Preparing the Table Data","1. Prepare the data for each interface table using the corresponding worksheet in this template. See the section Excel Template Format for details about this template.\n2. Refer to the bubble text on each column header either for detailed instructions on preparing the data in that column, or for a description of the data and data type that the column requires.\n3. Common tasks for preparing table data include setting up for data merge, and searching for internal identifiers.","Loading the Data","1.  After you finish preparing the data in the parent and child sheets, click the Generate CSV File button. The program generates both a CSV file and a ZIP file.  \n2.  Load the data using the Load Interface File for Import process:\n     1. Log in to the Oracle Cloud SFTP server.\n     2. Transfer the ZIP file to the SFTP server location.\n     3. Log in to Oracle Fusion Applications.\n     4. Navigate to Scheduled Processes.\n     5. Select the Load Interface File for Import process.  \n     6. Selec","Excel Template Format","• Each interface table is represented as a separate Excel sheet.\n • The first row in each sheet contains column headers that represent the interface table columns. The columns are in the order that the control file expects them to be in the data file. \n    Do not change the order of the columns in the Excel sheets. Changing the order of the columns will cause the load process to fail.\n    You can hide columns that you do not intend to use, but you cannot delete columns. Deleting columns will cau","Recommendations for Loading Standard Cost Data","Because the details of any data conversion will vary, the scope of this document is limited to a best practices approach. If you are new to data conversion, we recommend consulting Oracle resources on open interfaces and the strategies for populating them.\n\nIn general, we recommend the following:\n1) Build an export file in the same format as the Mass Additions interface described in this template. No matter which method you use to extract data, you will need to create staging tables and a spread","Importing the Loaded Data","After you successfully load your data, you must submit the Interface Standard Costs process to import the data into the application tables.\n\nTo submit the Interface Standard Costs process:\n  1. Navigate to the Scheduled Processes UI (under Tools).\n  2. Click on Schedule New Process and select 'Interface Standard Costs'.\n  3. Enter the appropriate parameter(s) and submit. \n  4. Monitor the process in the Scheduled Process UI.\n  5. If the submitted process ends in error or warning,  review the log"]};
